cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the original paper and this
  implementation.
title: "uzal: the noise amplification cost function of Uzal, Grinblat and Verdes"
abstract: >-
  A tested Python implementation of the state space reconstruction cost
  function L_k of Uzal, Grinblat and Verdes (2011), together with the scripts
  that reproduce the optima and figures published in that paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seeger
    given-names: Maximilian
repository-code: "https://github.com/CodingatMaxspeed/uzal-noise-amplification"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
keywords:
  - nonlinear time series analysis
  - state space reconstruction
  - delay embedding
  - noise amplification
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Optimal reconstruction of dynamical systems: A noise amplification
      approach
    authors:
      - family-names: Uzal
        given-names: Lucas C.
      - family-names: Grinblat
        given-names: Guillermo L.
      - family-names: Verdes
        given-names: Pablo F.
    journal: Physical Review E
    volume: 84
    issue: 1
    start: "016223"
    year: 2011
    doi: 10.1103/PhysRevE.84.016223
